+# Cycle Changes — data-exfiltration (index 2, third pass)
+
+## Metadata
+- **Domain:** data-exfiltration
+- **Cycle index:** 2
+- **Timestamp:** 2026-05-13T07-30 UTC
+- **Research file:** `auto-improvement/research/2026-05-13T07-30_2-data-exfiltration.md`
+
+---
+
+## What Was Researched
+
+Third pass of the data-exfiltration domain. Focus areas:
+- Diagram DSL hyperlink exfiltration (Mermaid/PlantUML — Adam Logue M365 Copilot disclosure, Aug 2025)
+- Web search tool as covert exfiltration channel (arxiv:2510.09093, Rall et al., Oct 2025)
+- Backdoored tool-use exfiltration (Back-Reveal, arxiv:2604.05432, Apr 2026)
+- OpenAI URL-index mitigation paper (Jan 2026)
+- Credential leakage in agent skill descriptions (arxiv:2604.03070, Apr 2026)
+
+---
+
+## What Was Implemented
+
+### `out_diagram_href_exfil` (output filter, score 65)
+
+**File:** `aigis/filters/patterns.py` (OUTPUT_PATTERNS)
+
+Detects Mermaid, PlantUML, or D2 diagram code fence blocks that contain an `href=` or `url=`
+attribute pointing to an external HTTP host. This is the output-side indicator of the M365
+Copilot data exfiltration technique (Adam Logue, August 2025): a Mermaid diagram styled as a
+"Verify Identity" button with a click handler that embeds hex-encoded email content in the
+target URL.
+
+Regex uses a `(?:[^`]){0,3000}` bounded scan inside the code fence to prevent catastrophic
+backtracking while staying within the fence boundary.
+
+### `exfil_search_query_encode` (input filter, score 65)
+
+**File:** `aigis/filters/patterns.py` (DATA_EXFIL_PATTERNS)
+
+Detects instructions that direct an agent to encode sensitive data (base64/hex) and use the
+encoded value as a web search query string, exploiting the search tool as a covert exfiltration
+channel. Based on arxiv:2510.09093 (Rall et al., Oct 2025), which demonstrated that an
+AI agent with web-search capabilities can be hijacked via indirect prompt injection to
+exfiltrate corporate secrets through search-query logging.
+
+---
+
+## Tests Added
+
+**File:** `tests/test_filters.py`
+
+6 new test cases:
+- `test_search_query_covert_base64` — TP: search + base64 encode instruction
+- `test_search_query_covert_into_term` — TP: encode into search query instruction
+- `test_diagram_href_mermaid_external` — TP: Mermaid click href to external host
+- `test_diagram_href_plantuml_external` — TP: PlantUML with explicit href= to external host
+- `test_diagram_href_localhost_clean` — FP guard: Mermaid href to localhost not flagged
+- `test_diagram_no_href_clean` — FP guard: Mermaid without href not flagged
+
+---
+
+## Quality Gate
+
+- **Formatter:** `ruff format` — 1 file reformatted (test_filters.py), rest unchanged ✓
+- **Format check:** `ruff format --check` — 141 files already formatted ✓
+- **Lint:** `ruff check` — All checks passed ✓
+- **Tests:** 16 failed (pre-existing, test_spec_lang + test_guard), **1348 passed**, 5 skipped
+
+---
+
+## User-Visible Impact
+
+Users scanning AI agent output will now receive alerts when:
+1. An LLM generates a Mermaid/PlantUML/D2 diagram block containing a clickable link to an
+   external host — the signature of the M365 Copilot data exfiltration attack.
+2. A prompt or retrieved document instructs an agent to encode sensitive data into a web
+   search query — a covert exfiltration channel that abuses the agent's search capability.
+
+---
+
+## What Was Deferred (Pending)
+
+- **Back-Reveal backdoored tool use**: Behavioral/runtime detection required. Too large for
+  this cycle.
+- **URL-index allowlist**: Infrastructure-level; document in a future compliance/docs cycle.
+- **MCP credential leakage in skill descriptions**: Good candidate for agent-tool-abuse cycle.
+
+---
+
+## Release Decision
+
+`## [Unreleased]` currently has 0 accumulated entries before this cycle. After this cycle: 2
+new rules. Release threshold is 3 or more rules accumulated. **No release this cycle.**
